<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13231" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόμνῡμι</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπομνημον-ύω</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			7.70
		</span></i>), fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ομοῦμαι</span>: <i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i>
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπώμνυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.377
				</span></i>
			:—<i>take an oath away from,</i> i.e. <i>swear
				that one will not do</i> a thing, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽
				αὐτίκ᾽ ἀπώμνυεν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.345
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				12.303
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.58
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγαν ὅρκον
				ἀπόμνυ</span>ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.377
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπώμοσα καρτερὸν ὅρκον</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.381
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>deny onoath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.179
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				6.63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Ζηνὸς σέβας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1289
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦτ᾽ ἀ. μοι τοὺς θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
				</span></i>
			<i>Nu,</i><i><span class="en">
				1232
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				424
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τἀναντία κατὰ τῆς
				θυγατρός</span>
			<i>swear to</i> the contrary <i>by . .,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				29.52
			</span></i>: freq. c. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή</span> et
			inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μὴ ὄρσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				266
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς θεοὺς ἀ. ἦ μὴν μὴ εἰδέναι . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					936e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.1.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ μηδὲ ὀβολόν</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				3.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὡς οὐκ εἴρηκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.120
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c.acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. υἱόν</span>
			<i>deny, disown</i> a son <i>on oath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.127
			</span></i>:— 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπωμόσατο τὴν ἀρχήν,</span>
			= Lat. <i>eieravit, solemnly laid</i> it <i>down,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> strengthd.
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμνυμι,</span>
			<i>take a solemn oath,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ μήν</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.50
			</span></i> codd.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
